{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling","id":1077489,"title":"Help me build a 2E Starting Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-12T20:58:41-07:00","id":1077489,"title":"Help me build a 2E Starting Changeling","content":"As the title said, I need help building a starting character from Changeling 2E's rules. I've never made a character before, so I need your help to make his stats better and some advice on what to give him to round him out.<br /> <br /> <b>Jace Floria</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Concept</b>: Terrifying Ninja<br /> Seeming: Darkling<br /> Kith: Brollachan<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 2, Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2, Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Skills</b>: Crafts 3, Medicine 1, Athletics 4, Brawl 3 (Gauntlets), Stealth 4 (Shadows), Intimidation 4, Empathy 3 (Fears)<br /> <br /> Health 7<br /> Willpower 5<br /> Defense 7<br /> Speed 11<br /> Initiative Mod: 7<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: Fighting Finesse (Grappling) (2), Area of Expertise (Shadows) (1), Interdisciplinary Specialty (Shadows) (1), Killer Instinct (3), Potent Kith (3), Mantle (Autumn) (1/Free)<br /> <br /> Wyrd 1<br /> Glamour 5/10 - 1 Glamour per turn<br /> <br /> <b>Contracts</b><br /> <b>Boon of the Scuttling Spider </b>(2)<br /> - Dice Pool: Dexterity + Athletics + Wyrd (9 +2 if Shadows Specialty Applies)<br /> - Success: Allows you to walk or run along any surface that can support your weight, even along walls and ceilings<br /> - Exceptional Success: Gain a +2 bonus to Dexterity<br /> - Darkling Clause: The character is surrounded by a shroud of darkness that extends 5 meters from her body. Anyone else acting within the shroud or attempting to attack someone within it suffers the Blind Tilt.<br /> - Catch: The character is following the path of an actual spider along the surface he is traveling.<br /> <b>Creeping Dread </b>(1)<br /> - Dice Pool: Manipulation + Empathy + Wyrd (6 +1 if Fear Specialty applies, +2 if Shadows Specialty Applies) Vs. Resolve + Wyrd (an average of 2 or 3)<br /> - Success: Target suffers a -(Wyrd) (-1) penalty to resist fear or Intimidation<br /> - Exceptional Success: Target suffers the Shaken Condition<br /> - Darkling Clause: Target also suffers the Spooked Condition<br /> - Catch: Contract is invoked while in the shadows<br /> <b>Night's Subtle Distractions </b>(2)<br /> - Dice Pool: Dexterity + Stealth + Wyrd (9 +2 if Shadows Specialty Applies)<br /> - Success: For the rest of the scene, targets suffer the changeling\u2019s Wyrd as a penalty to notice or spot her. The changeling can affect a number of targets equal to her successes on activating this Contract within a 50 ft. area.<br /> - Exceptional Success: The changeling can make Stealth-based actions reflexively<br /> - Darkling Clause: Gain an Exceptional Success with 3 successes<br /> - Catch: Contract is Invoked outdoors at night<br /> <br /> Seeming Blessing: <b>Clarity of Abandon</b><br /> Gain a free point of Clarity by making a bad choice for others.<br /> <br /> Seeming Curse: <b>A Shade's Distrust</b><br /> Lose a point of Clarity if you blindly tust anyone, even your closest friend<br /> Darklings never suffers penalties to their senses in the dark. They cannot see through a blindfold, but they can see perfectly with no light whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Kith Blessing (<b>Brollachan</b>)<br /> He gains half his Wyrd (2) to all rolls to establish a grapple (4 + 3 + 1 + 2 + 2 in Shadows) (10/12)<br /> Gains the 8-again quality to all Stealth rolls<br /> If he spends a point of Glamour once he has grappled someone, he can make a Presence + Intimidation + Wyrd (2 + 4 + 4) (10) vs. Composure + Wyrd roll. If successful, he can choose to inflict either the Insensate Tilt or the Frightened Condition on the target. A single target can only suffer from one of these at a time.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Stuff</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Mien</b>: Martyr (Would Do Anything For A Friend)<br /> <b>Mask</b>: Terror (Loves Scaring People)<br /> <b>Aspirations</b>: Be better at Stealth / Intimidation / Fighting (Long Term), Train Dual Wielding Pistols (Short Term), ??? (Short Term)<br /> <b>Court</b>: Autumn<br /> <br /> When he was young, Jace's life was filled with fear. Fear of the dark, the monster under his bed, of the things that lurk in the night. He was afraid of losing his friends, of being taken away from them. He always put on a brave face though, telling himself that there was nothing to worry about, that nothing was going to happen, that he was just paranoid.<br /> <br /> He was right to be afraid.<br /> <br /> He was taken by the Gentry at the age of 12. He was dragged into Arcadia as he screamed and screamed until his throat was raw, yet no one heard him.<br /> <br /> Either through coincidence or the Keeper\u2019s cruel sense of Irony, He became the monster in the dark, the thing that goes bump in the night. The thing keeping his fellow captives in their Keeper\u2019s Domain, the thing that kept them in line.<br /> <br /> And all through this he was still afraid, not of the dark where he lived, or the monsters that were his cohorts, or the other things that lurk alongside him, oh no.<br /> <br /> He was afraid of his Keeper, who forced him into this form.<br /> <br /> He was afraid of the Huntsmen, who dragged those few that got past him back.<br /> <br /> He was afraid of his friend\u2019s rejection, the friends he was still loyal to even after all that had happened to him.<br /> <br /> It was that last one that pushed him over the edge.<br /> <br /> He ran, as fast as he could. Ran from his fellow monsters, who were hounding him. Ran from his Keeper, who would try to take him back. Ran from Arcadia, his prison. Ran from his fellow captives, who he abandoned to save himself. He ran and ran until he reached the Hedge and found a way back. He was free, he had won.<br /> <br /> He returned to his home after all that has happened, and found an impostor had taken his place. His friends had never even noticed he was gone. Some suspected something had happened, but the impostor was a good enough imitation to not be suspected as such.<br /> <br /> He caught the impostor alone and faced him. The imitation was taken aback but displayed no outward sign of surprise or fear. He knew better though, he looked into the eyes of the thing that had stolen his life and saw fear, saw confusion, and conviction. He looked into the things eyes and knew that It\u2019s composure is simply a mask to hide from It\u2019s fears. He looked at the Fetch in the eye and saw that he would not let who he thought of as his friends come to harm. Jace looked at the Fetch and saw so much of himself.<br /> <br /> He took a long hard look at himself, at who he was, at what his life had become in his absence. Old friends had changed or moved away, siblings grew up and left, mementos from his childhood were sold or given away. He looked at his life and realized that it wasn't his anymore. Hadn't been for along time.<br /> <br /> He would have thought that he would be angry, at the Keepers who had taken him from his life, at the Fetch that had replaced him, at the friends and family that didn't even realize he was gone, but he wasn't. He just felt empty. He briefly considered killing the Fetch for this, but realized that it wouldn't solve anything. So, he left. He left his friends, his family, his what was life before he was taken and left the Fetch to take care of it.<br /> <br /> Some would say that him leaving behind everything from his past with a piece of his soul was poetic. He just thought it was sad.<br /> <br /> Now he travels the world, trying to find a new life, a new purpose. New friends to protect, a new home to defend, and through it all he seeks the strength needed to fight against the Keepers, against the Huntsmen. He seeks the strength to protect all that he holds dear. He seeks strength so that he wouldn\u2019t have to be afraid anymore.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>To Get During Play</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Equipment</b><br /> Rapier<br /> <b>Attributes</b><br /> Dexterity (5), Wits (4), Presence (3), Resolve (3), Composure (4), Manipulation (3)<br /> <b>Skills</b><br /> Occult (3), Weaponry (3), Stealth (5), Intimidation (5), Empathy (4), Brawl (5), Crafts (5), Athletics (5)<br /> <b>Specialties</b><br /> Fear (Empathy), Rapier (Weaponry)<br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> Hedgespun (Gauntlet/Rapier) (3+), Mantle (Autumn) (3+), Fair Harvest (Fear) (1+), Potent Kith (5), Fleet of Foot (1+), Fast Reflexes (1+), Fighting Finesse (Rapiers) (2)<br /> <b>Contracts</b><br /> Mirror Walk (3), Vainglory (Mantle of Terrible Beauty) (2+), Inanimate Communion (Usage Bonus) (1+), Might of the Terrible Brute (Elemental) (2), Light-Shy (2), Paralyzing Shudder (5)<br /> <b>Entitlement</b><br /> Pilgrims of the Endless Road<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edit: As an aside, it is currently 4/13, which got me thinking about Homestuck, which got me thinking about making Jace a 13 year old. I know that children are not allowed Attributes or Skills above 3, but how many skill dots should he have at 13?. I'm tentatively calling it as 10/6/4, and 2 Specialties.<br /> <br /> Edit2: So, as it turned out Potent kith only effects the Primary Kith, so I changed the Kith Blessings around. Draconic is now primary with Shadowsoul as secondary. This makes him less stealthy but tougher and more terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":".  Added Progression Goals cause those are Important 04-22-2017, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T04:42:09-07:00","id":1077634,"title":"","content":"I've seen some 13 year olds that do not look like 13 year olds, like they are big dudes, so they could have some a strength score over 3.<br /> <br /> Early puberty can be triggered by obscity, abuse/trauma, ingested chemicals, and possibly genetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T04:42:39-07:00","id":1077635,"title":"","content":"What court are you concidering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:55:29-07:00","id":1077737,"title":"","content":"could I bring in my own character and get some help too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T09:40:25-07:00","id":1077773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1077737#post1077737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could I bring in my own character and get some help too?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:43:39-07:00","id":1078049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1077635#post1077635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What court are you concidering?</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, i was considering making him Spring court, due to his tendency to suppress his negativity, but now I'm thinking either Autumn (Cause he basically specializes in causing Fear) or Windet (Due to the whole stealth thing). Leaning on Autumn, cause while he can hide well he mostly uses that to either find out what his enemies are afraid of, gas lighting them (move their stuff around without them knowing to freak them out), or jump scares.<br /> <br /> Y'know what?, definitely Autumn Court.<br /> <br /> Edit: As for other peoples characters, why not?, not like I own this particular thread. I just started it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 04-13-2017, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:05:19-07:00","id":1078097,"title":"","content":"Good choice, it helps that Autumn just got a preview so that would be a n interesting source of inspiration for your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T20:31:07-07:00","id":1078736,"title":"","content":"So I added a backstory for the guy, can you guys help me determine whats appropriate for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T15:45:42-07:00","id":1079090,"title":"","content":"Here's the character I was talking about. I'm trying to create a character focused on being a detective. But i don't want to be a Slewfoot, at least not at first, since I want it to be something he chose after Arcadia. My concept is a grizzled noir detective stuck in the unaging body of a child. I even got White Oak Dragon to make a homebrew kith called the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e/page18\">Orphanwretch</a> a while back. What I'm unsure on is Seemings, Contracts and general balancing of stats, skills and merits.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Jimmy Noir/James Richards<br /> <b>Concept</b>: lawful neutral noir detective stuck in the body of a child<br /> <b>Seeming</b>: Beast<br /> <b>Kith</b>: Orphanwretch/Tunnelgrub<br /> <b>Mask</b>: Detective (sorta like Scholar)<br /> <b>Mien</b>: Survivor<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3, Strength 1, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2, Presence 1, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Computer 1, Investigation 3, Athletics 1, Survival 1 (city streets), Larceny 2 (pickpocketing), Stealth 3, Persuasion 2, Empathy 3, Subterfuge 4 (looking innocent), Streetwise 1<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;\">Health: 6<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Speed: 12<br /> Initiative Mod: 7<br /> Defense: 5<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Small-Framed (no cost), Anonymity (1 dot) , Fleet of Foot (2 dots), Interdisciplinary </span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Specialty</span><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (Looking Innocent; 1 dot), Common Sense (3 dots), Dual Kith (2 dots), Language (1 dot; Spanish)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Wyrd</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: 1</span></span><br /> <b>Glamour</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: 10/1</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot;\"><b>Contracts</b></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: Pathfinder (1 dot), Fang and Talon (1 dot, senses), Reflections of the Past (1 dot), Boon of the Scuttling Spider (2 dots)</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Blessing</b>: Clarity of Abandon. Lost in the lies and oppression of society, a Beast has great difficulty making head or tales of the cultural landscape before her. She remembers, though vaguely, that there is a reason for many of the rules and laws that keep people civilized, but the importance of those reasons has faded away. Rules of society are only chains around her neck, and obedience to those old ways is suffocating. (Perhaps suffocating to everyone, but only the Beast is wise enough to notice.) Once per story, a Beast can flaunt a cultural taboo despite great personal cost, and regain a point of Clarity for free.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Curse</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: A Beast\u2019s Burden. Confinement is a fate worse than death to the Beast. She\u2019s experienced it already, and her spirit is simply too big to fit comfortably into bondage. A Beast can, of her own free will, enter into a Contract or Pledge or other more intimate acts of binding, but it chuffs her more than the average Lost. Forced confinement, especially the physical kind, is too much for her. Escaping bonds requires three Glamour instead of one. Once per story, if a Beast is confined or imprisoned, she suffers a Clarity breaking point.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Primary Kith </b><b>Blessing:</b> The Orphanwretch gains the Small-Framed Merit at no cost. Additionally, whenever another character succeeds in a Social roll against the changeling, the orphanwretch may reflexively spend a point of Glamour to inflict either the Guilty or Leveraged Condition on the character. Doing so also gives the orphanwretch a number of bonus dice equal to his Wyrd on his next Empathy, Persuasion, or Subterfuge roll against the character.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Secondary Kith Blessing:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The tunnelgrub can deform his body in truly grotesque ways; bending bones and popping joints out of place at will. His Wyrd applies as a penalty to all rolls to establish or maintain a grapple on him. Spend a point of Glamour to reduce his effective Size by his Wyrd until the end of the scene for purposes of squeezing through narrow gaps or tight spaces. As well, increase his Dexterity by one dot; this can exceed his normal maximum.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not totally sure how to translate his character into a Mien and MaskE<br /> <br /> EDIT: largely figured out Mien and Mask<br /> <br /> EDIT: love your backstory<br /> <br /> EDIT: new kith upped his dex by one dot. Someone please check I did the recalculations for derived stats right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-06-2017, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T05:25:19-07:00","id":1079334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1079090#post1079090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: love your backstory</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks!, I had just finished expanding upon his encounters with the Fetch and leaving everything behind. I have no idea how to improve your character though. Perhaps you have some tips for mine?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T07:01:58-07:00","id":1079351,"title":"","content":"Maybe if you knew his back story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T08:11:59-07:00","id":1079367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1079090#post1079090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the character I was talking about. I'm trying to create a character focused on being a detective. But i don't want to be a Slewfoot, at least not at first, since I want it to be something he chose after Arcadia. My concept is a grizzled noir detective stuck in the unaging body of a child. I even got White Oak Dragon to make a homebrew kith called the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e/page18&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Orphanwretch</a> a while back. What I'm unsure on is Seemings, Contracts and general balancing of stats, skills and merits.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Concept</b>: lawful neutral noir detective stuck in the body of a child<br /> <b>Seeming</b>: Beast<br /> <b>Kith</b>: Orphanwretch<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3, Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2, Presence 1, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Computer 1, Investigation 3, Athletics 2 (running away), Larceny 2 (pickpocketing), Stealth 3, Persuasion 2, Empathy 3, Subterfuge 4 (looking innocent), Streetwise 1<br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Health: 6<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Speed: 11<br /> Initiative Mod: 6<br /> Defense: 5<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Small-Framed (no cost), Anonymity (1 dot) , Fleet of Foot (2 dots), Language (Spanish; 1 dot), Interdisciplinary Speciality (Subterfuge; 1 dot), Common Sense (3 dots)<br /> <br /> <b>Wyrd</b>: 1<br /> <b>Glamour</b>: 10/1</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Contracts</b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: Dream 1, Fang and Talon 2 (rats)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Blessing</b>: Clarity of Abandon. Lost in the lies and oppression of society, a Beast has great difficulty making head or tales of the cultural landscape before her. She remembers, though vaguely, that there is a reason for many of the rules and laws that keep people civilized, but the importance of those reasons has faded away. Rules of society are only chains around his neck, and obedience to those old ways is suffocating. (Perhaps suffocating to everyone, but only the Beast is wise enough to notice.) Once per story, a Beast can flaunt a cultural taboo despite great personal cost, and regain a point of Clarity for free.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Curse</b>: A Beast\u2019s Burden. Confinement is a fate worse than death to the Beast. He\u2019s experienced it already, and her spirit is simply too big to fit comfortably into bondage. A Beast can, of his own free will, enter into a Contract or Pledge or other more intimate acts of binding, but it chuffs her more than the average Lost. Forced confinement, especially the physical kind, is too much for her. Escaping bonds requires three Glamour instead of one. Once per story, if a Beast is confined or imprisoned, he suffers a Clarity breaking point.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Kith </b><b>Blessing:</b> The Orphanwretch gains the Small-Framed Merit at no cost. Additionally, whenever another character succeeds in a Social roll against the changeling, the orphanwretch may reflexively spend a point of Glamour to inflict either the Guilty or Leveraged Condition on the character. Doing so also gives the orphanwretch a number of bonus dice equal to his Wyrd on his next Empathy, Persuasion, or Subterfuge roll against the character.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Left two dots of contracts free for Court when i choose it and two dots of merits free because I wasn't sure what kind of changeling merits I wanted, or whether I should keep them for a communal motley hollow. Also not totally sure how to translate his character into a Mien and Mask<br /> <br /> EDIT: love your backstory</div> </div> </div> </div> You get one dot of Mantle free for pledging an Oath to a Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T01:33:52-07:00","id":1079720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1079351#post1079351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe if you knew his back story?</div> </div> </div> </div>that could help, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T02:47:02-07:00","id":1079729,"title":"","content":"Alright, here it is then<br /> <br /> RP stuff<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">[<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=991213#post991213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know a lot about how he got into the Durance, though. He was a foster kid, always moving from one home to the next for as long as he can remember. He was the kid who everyone said looked shifty, or dangerous, or lazy or any number of other stereotypes. To survive that kind of life, you have to be the perfect kid, obedient and a good worker. Problem was, he never really could pull that off. Inevitably, the foster &amp;quot;parents&amp;quot; replaced him with other, cuter children; or he punched another kid after they made fun of his old clothes and his bad grades (not his fault he'd switched school districts halfway through the first semester); or he just ran away when the home situation got dangerous. It was not what anyone would call a happy childhood, but as he walked down the streets on the day before his 19th birthday, he could only think about how much worse it was going to be on the streets. He had a high school degree, the clothes on his back, a backpack, a phone and a little bag of all the money he'd saved over the years, but he didn't have a bank account or the credit to get a loan on an apartment. He was going to be on the streets. <br /> <br /> And this is where I kinda get lost and stuck. I have a concept for his Keeper, but not fleshed out. And I have little idea how he got caught or got out. I just have the concept of a bunch of Keepers who think of humans in the way that the worst of European missionaries thought of the native populations they &amp;quot;ministered&amp;quot; to. They are horrified by our primitive &amp;quot;normality&amp;quot; and see it as their duty to teach us civilization, otherwise known as the alien logic of faerie. So they're running a sort of Victorian Domby Hall/Work House Domain, but without any regard for Euclidean geometry or the laws of time and it's trying to teach you that you should be ashamed of thinking that gravity pulls you down instead of pushing you purple or just doing whatever the hell I want it to do. <br /> <br /> Drew a blank on how he escapes, but his post-durance life is where i started the character, so I know this part very well. His durance has stunted his growth and made him mentally a grizzled old cigar-smoking, hard-drinking noir detective, but forever physically stuck in the body of a child. With makeup and a fake beard, he can convince the gullibe for a little bit, but he supernaturally exudes this aura of &amp;quot;help this poor baby&amp;quot;. He makes money doing the kind of things private detectives in real life actually do, usually finding dirt on shady husbands or looking for runaway kids. He never meets the clients, doing all his business through a site that he's promoted as an urban legend through various fake accounts on various forums. But if you really need to find someone who doesn't want to be found, you come to him.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T03:24:41-07:00","id":1079735,"title":"","content":"For Mien and Mask, something related to his job perhaps?, like, he gets willpower for helping others with stuff and regains an entire pool by doing that with a signifigant sacrifice on his part.<br /> <br /> Another one would be running away, leaving those in need in their plight. Your character has the stats for it but i dont know if he wants to do that.<br /> <br /> Court is trickier, they are custom built for each city instead of certain kinds of court in certain parts of the world. I got Autumn 'cause it fits so well with his fearmongering abilities. I guess yours could be Winter, I guess, if you're still using the Seasonal Courts scheme from 1E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T06:18:26-07:00","id":1079764,"title":"","content":"Interdisciplinary Specialty requires you to specify a specialty, not a skill. That specialty would then apply to any relevanty rolls of any skill. So you should specify if the specialty you chose was Running or Looking Innocent.<br /> <br /> If you chose Running, you would get a +1 bonus to Athletics when running, a +1 to Stealth when doing so without drawing attention, or a +1 to Larceny when doing it while running. Looking Innocent would net you +1 to Subterfuge while insisting your innocence, +1 to Persuasion while doing the same, or +1 to Larceny when trying not to look guilty while stealing something, which may end up stacking with the Pickpocketing specialty for a +2 bonus.<br /> <br /> Now on to my character, Dual Kith seems to be a bit much so I'm considering doing away with it altogether and just make a custom Kith based on being a monster in the dark that scares others away. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:07:22-07:00","id":1079795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1079764#post1079764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interdisciplinary Specialty requires you to specify a specialty, not a skill. That specialty would then apply to any relevanty rolls of any skill. So you should specify if the specialty you chose was Running or Looking Innocent.<br /> <br /> If you chose Running, you would get a +1 bonus to Athletics when running, a +1 to Stealth when doing so without drawing attention, or a +1 to Larceny when doing it while running. Looking Innocent would net you +1 to Subterfuge while insisting your innocence, +1 to Persuasion while doing the same, or +1 to Larceny when trying not to look guilty while stealing something, which may end up stacking with the Pickpocketing specialty for a +2 bonus.<br /> <br /> Now on to my character, Dual Kith seems to be a bit much so I'm considering doing away with it altogether and just make a custom Kith based on being a monster in the dark that scares others away. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that there was a kith that might help with that in the preview documents. I think it was called the brollachan or something like that. I probably mangled the spelling on that one, but I'm responding on my phone so I'm going by memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:21:49-07:00","id":1079826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1079764#post1079764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interdisciplinary Specialty requires you to specify a specialty, not a skill. That specialty would then apply to any relevanty rolls of any skill. So you should specify if the specialty you chose was Running or Looking Innocent.<br /> <br /> If you chose Running, you would get a +1 bonus to Athletics when running, a +1 to Stealth when doing so without drawing attention, or a +1 to Larceny when doing it while running. Looking Innocent would net you +1 to Subterfuge while insisting your innocence, +1 to Persuasion while doing the same, or +1 to Larceny when trying not to look guilty while stealing something, which may end up stacking with the Pickpocketing specialty for a +2 bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely looking innocent for the specialty. It's basically hardcoded from Arcadia. You think i could swing using it for purposes like surprising people with attacks and such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-17-2017, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:23:28-07:00","id":1079828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1079795#post1079795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe that there was a kith that might help with that in the preview documents. I think it was called the brollachan or something like that. I probably mangled the spelling on that one, but I'm responding on my phone so I'm going by memory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are right. It wasthe brollachan and they were all about being intimidating torturers and guards. It's pretty perfect for your concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:31:52-07:00","id":1079834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1079826#post1079826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely looking innocent for the specialty. It's basically hardcoded from Arcadia. You think i could swing using it for purposes like surprising people with attacks and such?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could at least use it to get close enough to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T15:39:34-07:00","id":1080048,"title":"","content":"You're right. The fluff is already so perfect, why didn't I see this before. Theres no enhancement to Intimidation, but 8-again stealth and inflicting Insensate and Frightened makes up for it. Ill edit the character write-up as soon as I get out of school and on to a computer in like, ten hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:34:58-07:00","id":1080262,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a list of all the existing official and homebrew courts? Also, you don't have to be Asian to be in the Directional Courts, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:41:53-07:00","id":1080265,"title":"","content":"Just to check, Grappling needs Strength + Brawl right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:51:32-07:00","id":1080269,"title":"","content":"there's got to be some dexterity stuff involved. Strength + Brawl sounds like the roll for just punching someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T05:58:41-07:00","id":1080273,"title":"","content":"added 1 dot of Striking Looks (Adorable) to my character. What do you think of this choice? Also, any ideas on a name? My placeholder was Jimmy Noir, but it seemed too on-the-nose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:10:48-07:00","id":1080279,"title":"","content":"Just to checked, it's Strength + Brawl - Opponent's Defense, then a contested Strength + Brawl roll each action with the winner choosing a grappling move to use. So, assuming an average Defense of, lets say 3, with my guy having Brawl 3 and Strength 3. He rolls (3 + 3 + 2 - 4) (4) dice. The roll 6 dice to contest others. Maybe the bonus to establish Grapples shouldn't be halved?. I'll look at some merits, maybe theres one that makes Grappling use Dexterity instead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:19:34-07:00","id":1080284,"title":"","content":"'Kay, got some stuff. <br /> <br /> Choke Hold (2 dots) is an extra grappling maneuver. <br /> <br /> Fighting Finesse (2 dots) could do it with a Grappling Specialty.<br /> <br /> Defensive Combat (1 dot) Substitutes Athletics with either Weaponry or Brawl (chosen at purchase) to calcuale defense while those skills apply.<br /> <br /> Edit: Question: does Interdisciplinary Specialty stack with Area of Expertise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12398,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","user":"DArchon5","date":". 04-18-2017, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:25:34-07:00","id":1080287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1080273#post1080273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">added 1 dot of Striking Looks (Adorable) to my character. What do you think of this choice? Also, any ideas on a name? My placeholder was Jimmy Noir, but it seemed too on-the-nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see nothing wrong with that, provided that it's the name he chose for himself and not the one he was given at birth. It has a nice ring to it, so if you like it, keep it. If not, just go for something that you find appealing and that would sound good when the character is introducing himself.<br /> Example: one of my recurring characters (which I've incarnated into multiple game systems) is an invariably rat like private detective with delusions of film noir that calls himself &quot;Slate Radigan, P.I.&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:33:04-07:00","id":1080291,"title":"","content":"Hey, does kith blessings and specialties apply to Contract activation rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:38:52-07:00","id":1080293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1080291#post1080291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, does kith blessings and specialties apply to Contract activation rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:41:58-07:00","id":1080294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1080287#post1080287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see nothing wrong with that, provided that it's the name he chose for himself and not the one he was given at birth. It has a nice ring to it, so if you like it, keep it. If not, just go for something that you find appealing and that would sound good when the character is introducing himself.<br /> Example: one of my recurring characters (which I've incarnated into multiple game systems) is an invariably rat like private detective with delusions of film noir that calls himself &quot;Slate Radigan, P.I.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was looking for one given at birth that still sort of hinted toward his eventual life, 'cause the Wyrd is weirdly weird that way. How about James Richards? Yeach, I like that. Jimmy the Private Dick. (the accidental innuendo is why he prefers Jimmy Noir.)<br /> <br /> Edit: wait a second, a rat-like PI? Great minds think alike! Big fan of rats and I was going to use that new 2e idea about contracts being reflected in the mien to give him some rat whiskers to reflect the &quot;Fang and Talon 2 (rats) Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-18-2017, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:56:45-07:00","id":1080394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1080294#post1080294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was looking for one given at birth that still sort of hinted toward his eventual life, 'cause the Wyrd is weirdly weird that way. How about James Richards? Yeach, I like that. Jimmy the Private Dick. (the accidental innuendo is why he prefers Jimmy Noir.)<br /> <br /> Edit: wait a second, a rat-like PI? Great minds think alike! Big fan of rats and I was going to use that new 2e idea about contracts being reflected in the mien to give him some rat whiskers to reflect the &amp;quot;Fang and Talon 2 (rats) Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense. If he's a Beast, then he'd need some sort of animal features anyway.<br /> Radigan always has something tying him to rats, regardless of the incarnation. I've used him as a rat Beast and multiple types of wererats, amongst other things. The rats and the delusions of film noir are the traits that he always has, and I often enjoy reimagining him into new horror or urban fantasy settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T10:19:32-07:00","id":1080409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1080394#post1080394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would make sense. If he's a Beast, then he'd need some sort of animal features anyway.<br /> Radigan always has something tying him to rats, regardless of the incarnation. I've used him as a rat Beast and multiple types of wererats, amongst other things. The rats and the delusions of film noir are the traits that he always has, and I often enjoy reimagining him into new horror or urban fantasy settings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, the Beast thing. To be honest, I'm still not sure entirely how he escaped, so his Seeming and parts of his character are still largely in flux","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:37:41-07:00","id":1080456,"title":"","content":"just had a new backstory idea. His Keeper was in a feud with another Keeper known as the Rat King or something like that. The game was that The Elegant Institution tried to turn humans into civilised fairies, while the Regent of Filth tried to seduce the students to the wild, anarchic side of the fey. James defected to the Rat King's side, thinking it was a place for outcasts like him, until he realized it was just as poisonous as the Institution. That was when he tore out the part of him that desired the approval of others and used it to painstakingly dig a tunnel out of the foundations into the Hedge. <br /> <br /> This is making me consider making him an Ogre or a Darkling and possibly getting rid of Parkour to make him a dual kith with secondary Tunnelgrub. Also, rearranging skills","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T18:44:38-07:00","id":1080689,"title":"","content":"Okay, so now he Grapples using Dexterity, Presence and Manipulation are both at 2, gave him Crafts 3 cause he pretty much has zero uses for mental skills and I gave him Carpentry as a hobby, Larceny and Weaponry dots are redistributed between Athletics, Brawl and Stealth, Subterfuge was thrown out and replaced by Empathy, his Shadows specialty applies to any skill <i>and </i>grants a +2 bonus, finally he gets Night's Subtle Distractions and Boon of the Scuttling Spider in place of Light-Shy and Glimpse of a Distant Mirror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T20:46:45-07:00","id":1080727,"title":"","content":"Possible Breaking Point Triggers<br /> <br /> Jace Floria:<br /> * He was used to guard others in Arcadia, others who he ha abandoned to their fates. He faces a definite Breaking Point if he leaves anyone to a terrible fate without doing anything, even if doing so would benefit him.<br /> * His captivity in Arcadia had cost him one of the most important parts of his former life: his friends and family. He suffers a definite Breaking Point upon facing the people he had lost or upon losing a friend or family member.<br /> <br /> Jimmy Noir<br /> * Jimmy was a student of his Keeper in their attempts to 'civilize' him. He faces a definite Breaking Point when following certain rules enforced by his Keeper.<br /> * I have no idea what his second Trigger could be. It saind that it relates to something he lost in Arcadia, but i don't know whats appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T06:08:46-07:00","id":1080858,"title":"","content":"I know it was my idea, but got a question. What do you think distinguishes the behavior of of fairy Lords and ladies from anarchic common fey. but with both still seeming insane and unreal. Anyone know more about Victorian Lost? They had something like that going on with Gentry class wars and the cultural differences bergen urban and country Courts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T06:37:03-07:00","id":1080864,"title":"","content":"I have no Idea. But can you help me?, I'm thinking about moving Dexterity down to 3 and raising Strength instead to free up the Merit dots Fighting Finesse takes up so i can get more useful merits. Think this is a good Idea?, I'd probably get Fair Harvest (Fear) (2) which makes harvesting fear a Rote action while subtracting a success from all other emotions that are harvested. Rote means reroll all failed dice right?, or maybe Entering Strike (2) (If you inflict damage with a Brawl-based strike, you gain a dice bonus equal to the damage you inflicted to a subsequent grappling hold (or shihonage, if you know the Aikido Fighting Style) attempt. This must be your next attack. Drawback: Your Defense does not apply during the turn in which you attempt an entering strike.), or maybe even just using it to get Potent Kith (5).<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T07:56:13-07:00","id":1080894,"title":"","content":"Seems fine to me, though I'm not sure how rote actions work. Though does Autumn still get bonuses on harvesting fear glamour? <br /> <br /> So, I was thinking Summer Court for Jimmy to reflect how mad he is at the Gentry for leaving him physically as a child forever and to allow him to harvest Wrath from the quarreling couples who hire him. That leaves me with two questions.<br /> <br /> Can he still harvest Wrath if he never meets them directly, but hears their wrath in their voice or text through the phone and email?<br /> <br /> Do you think Autumn, where he could look for occult secrets that could restart his growth, would be a better fit? I'm just not sure how he would harvest fear. He's not exactly fear - inducing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:54:32-07:00","id":1081336,"title":"","content":"Depends, is Jimmy more concerned with growing up or with getting back at his Keeper. If you don't know you could get your ST and RP a prelude where he ponders this very decision","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T10:17:03-07:00","id":1081483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1081336#post1081336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends, is Jimmy more concerned with growing up or with getting back at his Keeper. If you don't know you could get your ST and RP a prelude where he ponders this very decision</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say he's more concerned with growing up, but payback would be nice. I feel like he might waffle between the two courts. Alas, I have no ST. I've just been brainstorming this guy in various permutations for the past year, looking for a game. Anyway, bunch of new questions.<br /> <br /> 1) I have a bunch of characteristics for his Mien: adorable, rat-like, scarred/otherwise marred and rough-looking. But I have no way to make them fit together, especially since I'm now trying out him as an Ogre and I need some appropriately Ogrish touches without losing the cuteness<br /> <br /> 2) If he goes to the Autumn Court, should I shuffle around some Mental dots so he can get a dot in Occult so he's no longer untrained? Or should I buy it during play, like I plan to do with Firearms?<br /> <br /> 3) I feel like there was a Persistent Condition called &quot;Just a Kid&quot; or something. It might have been a Flaw from 1e. Anyone else remember it? cause it sounds pretty good for my concept. Also, the rules on getting and using persistent conditions confuse me. Some help? I know you get beats when they hinder you, but not how you get them. Do you have to buy them?<br /> <br /> 4) Rose Bailey (developer) said on the forums that Changelings are going to have Touchstones that are mortal friends and loved ones and maybe places or ideals that Changelings are trying to use to rebuild a new identity for themselves. But I'm not sure how an adult who looks like a child and lives off the grid by necessity is going to get those contacts. Any suggestions for potential Touchstones?<br /> <br /> 5) and again, any help with Mask and Mien Anchors? I'm thinking Survivor for Mien possibly, and creating a variant of scholar called Seeker or Detective for Mask","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-20-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T00:31:46-07:00","id":1081741,"title":"","content":"1) ???<br /> <br /> 2) Well, I think it's alright as long as he really get Fear and Bargains. Take my guy for example, he is in Autumn not because of his Intelligence (his lowest Attribute) but because of how terrifying he is (I.E. Intimidation 4 and +2 in Shadows, and the fact that he is a Brollachan, some Changelings Prison Guard) and the fact that he knows how to figure out others fears (Empathy 3). His only real Mental Traits are Wits 3, Crafts 3, and Medicine 1. I, mean I might get Occult later on, one simply cannot hang around Autumn Court without getting some Magic Savvy and if he ever gets to Entitlement, he would get Pilgrims of the Endless Road (a Convert from 1E) and get a Kith that gives Mental Bonuses (like an Intelligence dot).<br /> <br /> 3) Well, there are Persistent Condition called Child and Adolescent i found around the forum. I'm probably using them if my idea of a Sburb Session (from Homestuck) with all sorts of Monsters ever goes anywhere (except ones like Demon and Mummy, those are really hard to justify as Paradox Clone Babies, so is Werewolf but I'm just going to ignore it and say Paradox). The first caps Traits at 3 (I'm letting each child get one Attribute in their Primary Attributes to 4 to exemplify why they are special) and grants Stealth bonuses against adults while penalizing interactions with them, the other just penalizes social against adults, they stack. As for Beats, Its written just under them. You can start with as many as you want, if the ST allows it, just ask them. It doesnt grant bonuses to Character Creation but the long term benefits may be worth it.<br /> <br /> 4) The Employer, the people you help, different people fill this role as long as they hire you.<br /> <br /> 5) Can't help you with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T11:54:05-07:00","id":1088810,"title":"","content":"back to the thread. Ive been thinking a lot about this guy and I have a chance of actually getting into a game now. So, here's my question. Jimmy's Icon represents the part of him that cared about what other people thought of him and wanted to fit in. Does this sound more like a Darkling's icon, an Ogre's Icon, or a Beast's Icon to you guys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T16:01:24-07:00","id":1088890,"title":"","content":"Can be any of them, really. You just have to ask yourself what Jimmy would do, would he do what needs to be done, would he solve all his problems with violence, or would he reenact his rebellion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:35:11-07:00","id":1088984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1077489-help-me-build-a-2e-starting-changeling?p=1088890#post1088890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can be any of them, really. You just have to ask yourself what Jimmy would do, would he do what needs to be done, would he solve all his problems with violence, or would he reenact his rebellion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Reenact his rebellion. You're right, he's totally a Beast","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}